BRUHAT BENGALURU MAHANAGARA PALIKE (BBMP)
SPECIAL COUNCIL MEETING - AGENDA & RESOLUTION RECORD
Meeting No: BBMP/COUNCIL/2024/SC-07
Date: 22-March-2024 | Venue: BBMP Council Hall, N.R. Square, Bengaluru

------------------------------------------------------------------
AGENDA ITEM 1: PROPERTY TAX REVISION FOR COMMERCIAL ZONES (FY 2024-25)
------------------------------------------------------------------
Proposing Authority: Commissioner, BBMP Revenue Division
Resolution Reference: BBMP/REV/2024/TAX/0445

1.1 BACKGROUND
Pursuant to the State Government directive under Government Order No. RD/112/2024, BBMP is required to revise the Annual Rental Value (ARV) for commercial properties across all wards to align with current market rates. The existing ARV schedule, last revised in 2019, results in significant under-collection of property tax relative to actual market rentals.

1.2 PROPOSED TAX REVISION - WARD-WISE IMPACT

Ward 150 (Bellandur Outer Ring Road):
- Current ARV Rate (Residential): Rs. 4 - Rs. 8 per sq ft per annum
- Proposed ARV Rate (Commercial C-2 Zone): Rs. 18 - Rs. 45 per sq ft per annum
- Effective increase: 325% to 462%
- Affected properties: 1,847 registered properties (340 residential reclassified, 1,507 existing commercial)

Ward 83 (Koramangala):
- Current ARV Rate: Rs. 12 - Rs. 28 per sq ft per annum
- Proposed ARV Rate: Rs. 22 - Rs. 55 per sq ft per annum
- Effective increase: 83% to 96%

1.3 FINANCIAL IMPACT
BBMP Revenue Department estimates additional annual tax revenue of Rs. 127 crore across all affected wards, with Ward 150 contributing Rs. 23.4 crore of additional annual collection.

1.4 HARDSHIP CASES
The Revenue Commissioner has identified that 1,200 small commercial tenants (monthly rent below Rs. 15,000) in Ward 150 will face proportionate rent increases as landlords pass through enhanced tax liability. No tenant protection scheme is proposed in this resolution.

RESOLUTION: The BBMP Council RESOLVES to adopt the revised ARV schedule effective 01-April-2024, subject to State Government approval.

Votes in Favour: 98 | Against: 34 | Abstained: 12

------------------------------------------------------------------
AGENDA ITEM 2: ROAD WIDENING ACQUISITION - OUTER RING ROAD EXTENSION
------------------------------------------------------------------
Proposing Authority: BBMP Engineering Department
Resolution Reference: BBMP/ENG/2024/RD/0221

2.1 PROPOSED ACQUISITION
Under the Karnataka Highways Act, 1964, BBMP proposes acquisition of 8.2 metres of land along both sides of the existing Outer Ring Road between Bellandur Junction and Sarjapur Road Junction (approx. 4.2 km stretch) for road widening from current 60m right-of-way to 100m right-of-way.

Estimated affected structures: 287 buildings (commercial and residential mixed).
Estimated displaced residents: 1,840 persons.
Compensation basis: Circle Rate as per guidance value under Karnataka Stamp Act.

2.2 OBJECTIONS ON RECORD
Ward 150 Residents Welfare Association filed objections (ref: BBMP/OBJ/2024/150/023) citing:
- Guidance value compensation is 40-60% below current market value.
- No rehabilitation scheme for displaced commercial tenants.
- Environmental clearance under the Karnataka Environmental Act not obtained.

RESOLUTION: The BBMP Council RESOLVES to proceed with acquisition process under Karnataka Highways Act, 1964. Joint Commissioner (Zoning) directed to constitute Land Acquisition Committee within 30 days.

Votes in Favour: 78 | Against: 54 | Abstained: 12

------------------------------------------------------------------
AGENDA ITEM 3: SOLID WASTE MANAGEMENT - WARD 150 SEGREGATION COMPLIANCE
------------------------------------------------------------------
Proposing Authority: BBMP Solid Waste Management Department
Resolution Reference: BBMP/SWM/2024/0089

3.1 COMPLIANCE STATUS
As of Q4 2023, Ward 150 shows 62% compliance with mandatory source segregation requirements under the Solid Waste Management Rules, 2016. The 38% non-compliant commercial establishments (approx. 456 units) have received three prior notices under Section 15 of the Karnataka Municipalities Act.

3.2 PROPOSED PENALTY
BBMP proposes imposition of Rs. 5,000 per month non-compliance penalty on commercial establishments that have failed to achieve source segregation within 60 days of notice.

RESOLUTION: BBMP Council APPROVES the penalty schedule. BBMP Commissioner directed to issue formal penalty notices within 15 days.

Votes in Favour: 143 | Against: 1 | Abstained: 0

------------------------------------------------------------------
AGENDA ITEM 4: BUDGET ALLOCATION - PARKS & PUBLIC AMENITIES (WARD 150)
------------------------------------------------------------------

4.1 PROPOSED ALLOCATION (FY 2024-25)
- Bellandur Lake Rejuvenation Phase 2: Rs. 8.5 crore
- Ward 150 Parks Maintenance: Rs. 1.2 crore
- Cycle Track Development (ORR stretch): Rs. 2.8 crore
Total: Rs. 12.5 crore

RESOLUTION: BBMP Council APPROVES the budget allocation. Tender process to commence within 45 days.

